---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { breadcrumbListSchema, articleSchema } from "../utils/schema";
const schema = [articleSchema("Best Forbidden City Photo Spots: 8 Top Locations 2026", "Discover the 8 best photo spots inside the Forbidden City: Hall of Supreme Harmony at golden hour, corner towers at sunset, hidden courtyards.", "2026-07-30"), breadcrumbListSchema([{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: "Photo Spots", url: "/photo-spots" }])];
---
<Layout
  title="Best Forbidden City Photo Spots: 8 Top Locations 2026"
  description="8 best photo spots inside the Forbidden City: Hall of Supreme Harmony at golden hour, Imperial Garden, corner towers at sunset, and hidden courtyards."
  canonicalURL="/photo-spots"
  schema={schema}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: "Photo Spots", url: "/photo-spots" }]}
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 pt-24 pb-16">
    <p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-imperial">Photo Spots</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-6xl">Top Photo Spots Inside the Forbidden City</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-lg text-charcoal">From the iconic Hall of Supreme Harmony to hidden courtyards, here is where to find the best shots.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-24">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-8">8 Best Photo Spots</h2>
    <div class="space-y-10">
      <div class="flex gap-4"><span class="mt-1 flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-sm bg-imperial text-xs font-bold text-white">1</span><div><strong class="font-medium">Hall of Supreme Harmony (Southeast Corner)</strong><p class="text-sm text-charcoal">The iconic shot. Position yourself at the southeast corner of the massive courtyard. Morning light (8:30-10:00 AM) illuminates the golden roof beautifully. Use a wide-angle lens to capture the full scale of the courtyard. Arrive at opening for crowd-free shots.</p></div></div>
      <div class="flex gap-4"><span class="mt-1 flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-sm bg-imperial text-xs font-bold text-white">2</span><div><strong class="font-medium">Northwest Corner Tower (Moat)</strong><p class="text-sm text-charcoal">The most photographed spot in Beijing. The northwest corner tower reflected in the moat at sunset is pure magic. Arrive an hour before sunset to claim your spot — dozens of photographers line up here daily. Best time: golden hour, any season.</p></div></div>
      <div class="flex gap-4"><span class="mt-1 flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-sm bg-imperial text-xs font-bold text-white">3</span><div><strong class="font-medium">Imperial Garden</strong><p class="text-sm text-charcoal">Ancient cypress trees (some 600 years old), rockeries, and ornate pavilions. Photograph in the late afternoon when soft light filters through the trees. The twisted cypress near the north gate is a favorite subject.</p></div></div>
      <div class="flex gap-4"><span class="mt-1 flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-sm bg-imperial text-xs font-bold text-white">4</span><div><strong class="font-medium">Gate of Supreme Harmony Courtyard</strong><p class="text-sm text-charcoal">The vast marble courtyard creates dramatic scale. Use a wide-angle lens (16-24mm) to capture the full expanse with people for scale. Best in the morning when shadows create depth.</p></div></div>
      <div class="flex gap-4"><span class="mt-1 flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-sm bg-imperial text-xs font-bold text-white">5</span><div><strong class="font-medium">Eastern Side Halls</strong><p class="text-sm text-charcoal">Escape the crowds. The red pillars and intricate painted beams in the eastern corridors offer beautiful architectural details. Far fewer tourists, much better photos. Late morning light creates dramatic shadows on the red columns.</p></div></div>
      <div class="flex gap-4"><span class="mt-1 flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-sm bg-imperial text-xs font-bold text-white">6</span><div><strong class="font-medium">Jingshan Park Overlook (Outside, North Gate)</strong><p class="text-sm text-charcoal">Not technically inside, but the single best panoramic shot of the Forbidden City. Climb to the hilltop pagoda after your visit. Late afternoon gives the best light on the golden roofs stretching south. Entry 2 CNY — the best value photo in Beijing.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  
  </section>

</Layout>
